<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Most wheat bids rise.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Most wheat bids rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most cash bids for spring, white and hard red winter wheat were higher in reaction to higher prices at the major U.S. wheat futures markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>A few dealers reported buying small quantities of wheat Thursday, but elsewhere farmers were awaiting higher prices.</p>
<p>Montana sources said farmers seek $4.15 per bushel for hard red winter wheat, about 15 cents higher than local bids.</p>
<p>Northern Montana dealers said four to five inches of snow fell Thursday, slowing farmer selling but adding needed soil moisture.  </p>
